  "qualification": "239 core tests, 15 integration tests and 3 doctests pass. Strict all-feature/all-target Clippy, warning-denied rustdoc, WASM library build, fuzz-bin strict Clippy, both formatting checks and both release benchmark builds pass. Six kernel benchmark processes retain all 66 receipts; five scope-cost processes retain all four rows and exact-answer/usage assertions.",
  "regression_scope": "Seven new integration tests cover actual BREP five-root parameter location and retry, shared nested limits, smaller child failure, cheap/warm results and domain errors, strict ambient-policy isolation, unwind accounting and Hypercurve promotion failure/retry. Two deliberate mutants fail focused assertions. The new documented constructor example compiles and runs.",
  "source_review": "OperationContext is immutable reusable configuration. evaluate composes existing Hypersolve with_budget with the existing strict BREP scope; no new counters or alternate error model are added. Existing geometry algorithms and kernel benchmark source are unchanged. The broader WorkLimits design remains a future instrumentation target.",
  "limits": [
    "Only existing instrumented solver refinements and algebraic promotions are counted; scalar precision, all geometry/elimination work, degree/coefficient growth, memory and time are not bounded.",
    "Scopes are synchronous and thread-local. Worker allocations, cancellation and async propagation are not implemented. Callback side effects are not rolled back.",
    "The result preserves callback errors and uncertainty but does not certify arbitrary caller calculations. Detailed proof-stage receipts and mandatory composed provenance remain open.",
    "The five-root fixture uses exact dyadic roots. It does not qualify non-materializable algebraic BREP topology or complete WP02.",
    "Timing and RSS samples are descriptive; allocation counts and statistical significance are not claimed. Direct/scoped ratios include additional scope setup, charging and usage checks.",
    "WASM and fuzz targets compile; no new WASM execution, fuzz/lexicase or ASan campaign, full workspace or pre-push qualification is claimed. All work-package completion gates remain open."
  ],
